# A crafting will plans through the master's leave
#
# The smelter's will, standing in the smith's forge with a charcoal rake, wants to work a forge hearth —
# and the only one is the smith's, which waits on his leave. The planner takes the conversation as a step
# on the way (its outcome, the leave, is known in advance), so the plan is two steps: ask the smith for
# the smithy, then set to work at the hearth.
#
# (Not the blacksmith: his will has the ruin's ownerless anvil two steps away as well — out of the door
# and to work — and between two equally short ways the plan keeps the one it met first.)
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --grant-mm smelting --grant-item charcoal_rake --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Forge" --period dawn

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

expect-state will will smelting steps=2
expect-state will for the use of the test smithy
expect-state will set to work at the test forge hearth
expect-state will aim=1/5
quit
